column2:
[ ... ] let us sit down(?), just we two alone;
7	[ ... ] the star [ ... ]
8	[ ... ] let us sit down, just we two alone.

By your main strength you have slain the warden —
21-22a	what can bring shame on you(?)? Lay the forest of <cedar> low!
22b	Seek me out a towering cedar
22c	whose crown vies with the sky:
23	I will make a door a reed-length broad;
24	let it have no pivot; let it travel in the socket;
25	its side a cubit(?), a reed-length its breadth;
26	let no stranger come near it; let a god del[ight in it.]
27	To the house of Enlil the Eu[ph]rates shall carry it;
28	let the crowd of Nippur rejoice over it;
29	let Enlil delight in it!
